&lt;h2&gt;About the role: What&#39;s in the Box&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Logistics Tribe builds the systems powering end-to-end delivery across North America, Europe and Australia/New Zealand: getting fresh ingredients into our facilities, giving customers the best delivery options the network can support, and tracking every box to the customer&#39;s door. Today it is a single engineering team - two staff engineers, a data engineer and seven mid-to-senior engineers - led by the Director of Engineering, owning that software and keeping it running in production. You will join as an Engineering Manager and take line management of the seven.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work is operations-heavy and business-critical, spread across different subdomains. You won&#39;t own a fixed backlog in one corner of the domain; the team&#39;s scope follows where the business pressure is. That is reflected in how we work: rather than one fixed squad, the team organises into small, project-focused pods that form and dissolve as projects start and finish. In a typical sprint, your engineers might be spread across three projects with three different product managers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategy and technical direction are things we shape together - staff engineers, product managers and you all contributing, nobody working from a script handed down. You own the people and the delivery of your engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role reports to the Director of Engineering for Logistics Tech; your team is spread across two geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
